{
  "id": "ch4",
  "title": "THE SINK",
  "objPage": "S8A1",
  "preset": "drowned",
  "notes": [
    "CAMPAIGN.md §8.1 / §12.2 '4-1'..'4-6'. The one deliberate return (D4): every area is a returnVisit (ARCHITECTURE §3.8) with the drowned palette on every slice and >= 25% of its cells patched (broken-tank dynamic cells of E8a0, rock collapses, standing water, scaffolds, pump pipes, the capsule removed, the cut floor).",
    "E8a1 past 2992 (CAMPAIGN 4-1, 4-3) is not used: the original camera falls there during a fade (segment 0x09 at 3008), its terrain is type 0 in every row (no lane was authored) and its scroll2 is empty from X 3100, so a lane there would stand on nothing. E8a1 elsewhere has a 32-px wading lane (live h 784-815), except the sluice basin 1504-1664 (live top h 879-880, probed by work/re/runs/wpe-depth-e8a1): the basin is what ch4 uses of E8a1 (4-3 and 4-6).",
    "4-1: the tunnel is E7a0 only (1792-2304, 2560-2800, 1792-2304 flip) and ends on the tunnel's own brick pier and arch (E7a0 1712-1792 flip continues the mirrored piece seamlessly) where the Bio Lab begins. The pump pipes of 4-3..4-6 are the E7a3 riser and elbows (E7a3 816-912, palette row 4 lifted); the first build's E4a2 'pipe' patches were empty cells that erased the cave art (gate 1 now warns on such patches).",
    "4-3: the sluice basin (E8a1 1504-1664) between two scaffold posts is the Brood Mother pool (the pit rect sits at its back); E8a2 1792-2304 before it and 1952-2304 after it, which continues straight into 4-4's E8a2 2304-2816; 4-4 ends on a mirror join (E8a2 2304-2816 flip).",
    "4-5: E8a3 3824-3968 has a 32-px lane (the throne-room entry narrows between rocks), so the chamber is E8a3 3968-4304, its mirror, then the throne E8a3 4400-4752 (capsule cells replaced, the floor in front of the steps cut open). 4-6: the basin, the cave arches E8a2 1920-2432 and their mirror (E8a2 1952-2432 flip), so the boss lock 1792-2176 is E8a2 columns only (E8a2 has no boss window).",
    "Seams (CAMPAIGN §4.1 join chunks): joins in the tunnel and the lab are covered by the tunnel's brick pier (E7a0 1760-1792, palette row 27 lifted), joins in the caves by a scaffold post (the propped timber of the E6a0 mine portal, E6a0 864-896, rows 9/8/3/2 lifted); every other join is a mirror join or continues the source.",
    "KI1 framing: E8a2 1792-3328 is framed at camY 256 (h 272-496), where the original camera stands there; at the §4.1 camY 512 the frame is the empty rock above the cave. Lanes checked live: E8a2 and E8a3 by work/re/runs/wpe-depth-e8a2 (it walked on into E8a3), E8a0 by stg-depth-e8a0; E7a0 1792-2832 is ROM terrain only (the probe stopped at the 1408 lock).",
    "Return-visit lock layout (§3.8): no lock window may start within 64 px of an original lock trigger of its source (E7a0 432/1408/1936/2352, E8a0 288/720/1152, E8a1 416/880/1392/2112/2560, E8a2 0/1840/2304, E8a3 4384), checked by gate 4.",
    "Far layer: one per section (4-1 E7a0, 4-2 E8a0, 4-3/4-4 E8a2, 4-5 E8a3, 4-6 E8a2); the open floor under the E8a3 bridge shows E8a3's own machinery far layer, as in the original (gate 2 warning).",
    "Section casts (CAMPAIGN §4.4 'cast', merged over the chapter pool): lighter A/BOMB/KNIFE variants where the ROM-affine HP budget of the chapter's waves exceeded ENEMIES §2.6 by more than 15% (tests/campaign.cjs (8)); ratio now 1.138.",
    "The drowned preset (flood + ruin + night 0.8) leaves the tunnel and the Bio Lab nearly black on the review sheet, so the chapter adds a lift (lightness x1.45, saturation x1.1) after it.",
    "4-1: the collapse where Hannah fell is the E8a2 rock fall over the tunnel ribs (an E4a0 rubble patch was tried: its cells carry the sea wall, not the heap)."
  ],
